From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:05:43 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ws-input

WonderSwan games get the console's two 4-way pads. slot is the only
mapper (the core's keymap is off), and the map is applied in the
emulator thread, frame by frame:

- Horizontal games: the D-pad is the X pad, A, B and START are
  themselves, and X and Y are turbo A and B. Holding L turns the D-pad
  into the Y pad; holding R turns the face diamond (X up, A right, B
  down, Y left) into the Y pad; both at once drive it from both
  clusters. L, R and SELECT never reach the game.
- Vertical games, upright: the D-pad is the Y pad and the face diamond
  the X pad, both turned so up is the game's up, and L and R are A and
  B, the core's own portrait map.
- A SELECT tap on a vertical game turns it to the landscape view with
  the horizontal map, and the next tap turns it back; SELECT with any
  other button, SELECT+X included, does not. Horizontal games ignore
  it. The view lasts for the session; every boot starts upright.

The modifier scheme follows nelynes/slotPlus
(https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/69b8379), the vertical
controls its 0f895d3 and SELECT doing nothing on horizontal games its
2ab147a (all GPL-3.0); the code is ours.
